{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent","id":1466815,"title":"[Crazy ideas] What would you want out of a 2ed of The Descent ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-05T13:49:34-07:00","id":1466815,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [Crazy ideas] What would you want out of a 2ed of The Descent ?","content":"So, Demon's finally been translated in French, which makes it tremendously easier for me to understand it !<br /> <br /> it is, therefore, the best time to ask you folks what you'd want out of an hypothetical 2nd edition of that awesome game.<br /> <br /> I'm still in the middle of reading the corebook (I read it long ago in English but I clearly didn't understood all of it back then and I hadn't as much experience as today when it comes to CoD games, since I'm now a very happy player in a Werewolf campaign !).<br /> <br /> Something I'd like personally would be to incorporate the Analysts wholly into the main book, add a new kind of Embeds and Exploits tailored to them and generally speaking (perhaps because I've read far too much Requiem) makes something a little more distinct with the Incarnations, which, I think should work a little like the Clans, in that they could give out one point in an Attribute or two to represent the way the God-Machines builds its angels.<br /> <br /> Then again, it is true that the corebook emphasis time and again that not all Destroyers are brutes and the like but I still think there could be something more here to mechanically adds more weight to the demon's time as an angel in the player's creation of her character, you know ? It wouldn't be too hard to tie it into the Speciality which can fray the Cover : Mary the gentle housewife actually knows how to wield a sword and the also is far stronger than her husband, but does her best to hide it all, as an exemple.<br /> <br /> I'd definitvely keep the Integrators as an Agenda. In most other splats, they are the &quot;low-level&quot;/evil/twisted version of the players, the one willing to seel other Changelings to the Fae or they would be VII or the Pure... But here, they are playable and it's actually one of the greatest strength of the splat for me. All Agendas would deserve to be expanded and worked upon to be more flesh out but Integrators are the one which needs it the most to me because of their almost bad-guys vibe.<br /> <br /> I also think that, in accordance with the Analysts becoming a base Incarnation, the Tempters would need to be split into two distinct Agendas : the good old hedonistic Tempters and Usurpers. The former would largely be the basic corrupt and self-serving demon which often spring into mind when ones think about the Tempters, whereas the Usurpers would be demons who truly believe that they are embryonic God-Machines in their own rights and who want to overthrow a tyrannic parent who stiffle their growth.<br /> <br /> I'll probably have more ideas as I read the book, but what would <b>you</b> want out of a potential 2ed ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 11-12-2021, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T14:16:27-07:00","id":1466817,"title":"","content":"Angels using demon rules. That\u2019s the tweet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T14:28:31-07:00","id":1466818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1466817#post1466817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels using demon rules. That\u2019s the tweet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or at the least, Bunyip being allowed a section to explain angelic cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T14:34:49-07:00","id":1466819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1466817#post1466817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Angels using demon rules. That\u2019s the tweet.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean instead of Numina, Inspirations and the like ?<br /> <br /> I'm not reading about Angel's rules yet (even if they were in the God Machine Rules Update which was also translated and much welcome for me to finally understand ephemeral beings!) but I guess them using Exploits, Embeds and the likes, even without a cost for their Cover would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T17:54:15-07:00","id":1466845,"title":"","content":"There was an <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition\">old thread</a> on this subject, from which my views largely haven't changed.<br /> - Clearer view from the start on how angelic Covers work, as stated<br /> - Possibly draw on Deviant's Web of Pain for rules for higher-level projects and infrastructure?<br /> - Streamline pact rules. They're structured with the detailed, customizable shape of 1e Changeling pledges, but not actually customizable and flexible enough to take advantage of that detailed system. There's no need to be weighing pact factors and modifying Willpower costs based on the imbalance.<br /> - Reduce Condition bloat. Demon doesn't have it as bad as some other gamelines but they can stand to be shorn down.<br /> - Demon, especially the corebook, suffers a little from a bias towards presenting angels and demons in an immediate context, defined by their most recent mission, in a manner that elides angels that have been active for historical events. At its worst, this can send the message that angels are minted for a particular mission and then stripped for parts or wiped of memory. Part of the appeal of a Demon game is in a character who has had some role in crafting the world as it is. More examples, then, of angels who have been reused for multiple projects across long stretches of time, such that you can play a recently fallen demon and say &quot;I appeared as dazzling lights over 12th century France&quot; as a background detail and have it make sense. I may be the one person really carrying this torch, but it matters to me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T23:30:20-07:00","id":1466908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1466845#post1466845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was an <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1355836-what-would-you-change-if-demon-the-descent-got-a-new-edition&amp;quot;]old</a> thread[/URL] on this subject, from which my views largely haven't changed.<br /> - Clearer view from the start on how angelic Covers work, as stated<br /> - Possibly draw on Deviant's Web of Pain for rules for higher-level projects and infrastructure?<br /> - Streamline pact rules. They're structured with the detailed, customizable shape of 1e Changeling pledges, but not actually customizable and flexible enough to take advantage of that detailed system. There's no need to be weighing pact factors and modifying Willpower costs based on the imbalance.<br /> - Reduce Condition bloat. Demon doesn't have it as bad as some other gamelines but they can stand to be shorn down.<br /> - Demon, especially the corebook, suffers a little from a bias towards presenting angels and demons in an immediate context, defined by their most recent mission, in a manner that elides angels that have been active for historical events. At its worst, this can send the message that angels are minted for a particular mission and then stripped for parts or wiped of memory. Part of the appeal of a Demon game is in a character who has had some role in crafting the world as it is. More examples, then, of angels who have been reused for multiple projects across long stretches of time, such that you can play a recently fallen demon and say &amp;quot;I appeared as dazzling lights over 12th century France&amp;quot; as a background detail and have it make sense. I may be the one person really carrying this torch, but it matters to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be great. Overall I think Demon would need a clearer view of what its Angels are. There is plenty of cases where it's said they have been active for centuries in the first chapter but it kind of contradict the idea that they generally fall on their first mission.<br /> <br /> I think a good way to reconcile the to would be for the Angels' ego to work more like a Windows version, sort off. That way an Angel could have lived for centuries but could also have a distance with his previous &quot;versions&quot;. Example : &quot;The 1.234 of me was whispering to Joan of Arc and guiding her because the God-Machine needed this and that but before my Fall I was the version 1.754 so I can't really remember how I felt about it initially&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, it'd need to go with a clearer view of what Covers are for Angels. As far as I understand it (haven't reached that part of the book) it seems to be unfrayable because it is sustained by an Infrastructure linked to the God-Machine which basically plaster over the cracks. However, unlike a Demon's it can be stolen and it prevent the angel from even manifestying on Earth.<br /> <br /> That last bit is neat but it'd need more explaining. Does an Angel built with a cover in mind doesn't come to live if demons jack it? Does it fall/become a monstrous Exile ? Shouldn't it manifest in his angelic body then ? <br /> <br /> Clearer explanations about it would be great. No need for additional rules, just more lore would already satisfy me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T02:40:05-07:00","id":1466919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1466818#post1466818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or at the least, Bunyip being allowed a section to explain angelic cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm working on my own version of this that basically uses possession rules as a foundation with infrastructure preparing an empty shell. <br /> <br /> But mostly I agree that angelic cover needs to be more defined so that a spy vs spy angle can be played up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T13:51:48-08:00","id":1467107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1466919#post1466919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm working on my own version of this that basically uses possession rules as a foundation with infrastructure preparing an empty shell. <br /> <br /> But mostly I agree that angelic cover needs to be more defined so that a spy vs spy angle can be played up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bunyip's explanation is simpler, cleaner*, and thoroughly more in line than I think a possession system would offer. And also leaves open angelic possession and claiming <br /> <br /> *Or at least that's how it makes me feel tonight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T14:39:56-08:00","id":1467111,"title":"","content":"Oh <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> , I don't think I've seen that post, what was their interpretation like?<br /> <br /> I'm still working on cleaning up mine but it largely is just possession rules with some minor tweaks like duration lasting longer than a scene and potentially having access to numen as an exception. Largely I feel that possession rules give a good foundation to work off of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T17:00:53-08:00","id":1467123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1467111#post1467111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> , I don't think I've seen that post, what was their interpretation like?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1023592-angelic-cover\">his posts in a thread you made</a> and there's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/985945-how-can-demons-pierce-angelic-cover?p=986779#post986779\">this post from a discussion of how to pierce angelic Cover</a> as far stuff that turned up on a site:-type search for &quot;bunyip angel cover&quot; (no quotes).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1467107#post1467107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Or at least that's how it makes me feel tonight.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly hard to let it go, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T00:23:29-08:00","id":1467332,"title":"","content":"So, continuing my reading of Demon, I can tell I like Embeds very much like they are. Some of them may need a rewrite to not be as broken as they seem to be at first glance (Fungible Knowledge and that other one which allows to switch Competences come to mind) but overall I feel they wouldn't need much work in a potential new edition.<br /> <br /> The Cypher on the other hand... I like the concept of it, of course, but I feel it has two huge flaws : it takes some agency out of the player character since it's basically designed by the Storyteller and it add a lot of weight on said Storyteller's shoulders because he has to design the Final revelation and the Interlocks. And he needs to do that basically before first session, once each character has been created but isn't really established. And if a player want to make changes/take his character in widly different directions it may invalidate the whole Cypher (I know I did just that with my Irraka, who started a Ghost Wolf and is drifting toward joining the Bone Shadows).<br /> <br /> Not losing the deep implications of the Cypher is hard because letting it to the player's appreciation means that min-maxers could very well end being Primum 4 with their whole Cypher super fast, knowing which Embeds to buy to unlock it. It's honestly a conundrum i'm hitting my head on and I can't seem to find a way to make it work better. So, would you guys keep it as such or do you have other ideas ?<br /> <br /> Addendum with Pactes : they are great conceptually but quite unwieldy in nature it seems, at least at a first reading, I'll need to return to it. The rules themselves are good for mortals but I find the Cover part to be somewhat too limited because the effects of the normal pacts don't extend far enough. In a future edition i'd like for them to perhaps provide a lesser number of dots but extend further so everyone would believe that something happened to the demon, if you get what I mean. Not sure I've the vocabulary to explain what I mean however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 11-10-2021, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T05:55:29-08:00","id":1467435,"title":"","content":"Thinking on it, I think I'd like to see demon approach the fate mechanics again. Though it could be as simple as taking what made it into the 2e core blue book I can't help but feel itd be different with a more active involvement from the god machine.<br /> <br /> Potentially related to that or possibly independent I think itd be interesting to see rules for people being pieces of infrastructure. Not simply people that work in infrastructure but people who are made to be pieces of infrastructure. This could be as simple as implanted routines that act like obsessions to fulfill an occult matrix. As for how much aether could potentially be stored in this unique infrastructure type, I'd probably lean on VtR ghoul mechanics and each human in such a network would only be able to store up to their stamina in aether.<br /> As an interesting side detail, such people could also potentially be made subhorned infrastructure by reprogramming their obsession and disconnecting them from the machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T03:53:52-08:00","id":1467533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1467435#post1467435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thinking on it, I think I'd like to see demon approach the fate mechanics again. Though it could be as simple as taking what made it into the 2e core blue book I can't help but feel itd be different with a more active involvement from the god machine.<br /> <br /> Potentially related to that or possibly independent I think itd be interesting to see rules for people being pieces of infrastructure. Not simply people that work in infrastructure but people who are made to be pieces of infrastructure. This could be as simple as implanted routines that act like obsessions to fulfill an occult matrix. As for how much aether could potentially be stored in this unique infrastructure type, I'd probably lean on VtR ghoul mechanics and each human in such a network would only be able to store up to their stamina in aether.<br /> As an interesting side detail, such people could also potentially be made subhorned infrastructure by reprogramming their obsession and disconnecting them from the machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitively be interesting ! Peoples are hinted at being importants for the God-Machine, so them being a form of Infrastructure could work very well. Bonus point, it'd make replenishing Aether both easier (you just have to observe and follow the humans who are parts of the Infrastructure) and deadlier (those guys are probably protected by Guardian Angels).<br /> <br /> What is the fate mechanism by the way ?<br /> <br /> Also, reading the Angels/Exile sections and it really bothers me that those guys have Numina and are basically Spirits. I feel it creates somewhat of a dichotomy between them and Demons which isn't necessarily needed and it contradict the idea that Embeds are just subroutines put in place by the God-Machine. If he created Embeds, why the hell wouldn't its servants have access to them ? I think it'd work better if Angels used Embeds and Deeper Embeds, subroutines which simply can't be accessed by Demons because they are tied to close to the God-Machine itself, if it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 11-12-2021, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T04:14:07-08:00","id":1467535,"title":"","content":"Fate: Everyone was originally supposed to have a Fate, which iirc was something like the God-Machine\u2019s designs and plans for them. A lot like people-as-Infrastructure, really. It was ultimately scrapped, and iirc got reworked into the Destiny Merit in Mage.<br /> <br /> Embeds &amp; Angels: Well I think the relationship between Angelic Numina and Demonic Embeds are like that between spirits\u2019 Numina and Uratha Gifts. Powers ultimately from the same source, but expressed differently because the channel is different.<br /> We kinda have \u2018deeper Embeds\u2019 already, as angelic Incepts and demonic Exploits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T06:52:00-08:00","id":1467556,"title":"","content":"As 21C hermit said but fate is also an optional system in blue book core was developed. Though in that its basically &quot;how will I die&quot; as a kinda 4th aspiration. It also plays into the numen fate sense. But that still feels like it falls short in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T08:07:54-08:00","id":1467562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1467535#post1467535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate: Everyone was originally supposed to have a Fate, which iirc was something like the God-Machine\u2019s designs and plans for them. A lot like people-as-Infrastructure, really. It was ultimately scrapped, and iirc got reworked into the Destiny Merit in Mage.<br /> <br /> Embeds &amp; Angels: Well I think the relationship between Angelic Numina and Demonic Embeds are like that between spirits\u2019 Numina and Uratha Gifts. Powers ultimately from the same source, but expressed differently because the channel is different.<br /> We kinda have \u2018deeper Embeds\u2019 already, as angelic Incepts and demonic Exploits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, just change Fate to &quot;purpose&quot; and you could easily re-flavor it from the destiny merit beyond simple mechanics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T15:15:00-08:00","id":1467603,"title":"","content":"Isn't it explicitly stated that Embeds (and Exploits?) are how demons access Numina (and Influences?) now that they're no longer connected to the G-M?<br /> You could compared it to Werewolf Gifts, but that breaks down pretty soon because Gifts are not meant to be a transfer or translation of any specific power a particular spirit has. A werewolf earning or stealing a Gift is just tapping into that spirit's symbolism, letting their own innate werewolf power be flavoured by the spirit's/Gift's concept.<br /> <br /> The Doylist answer is probably that the rules for angels were written to fit in the GMC, and thus it was both easy and economical (considering wordcount) to make them part of the revamped and unified ephemeral entity rules system. If DtD had come much later, I'd expect angels to be a lot more like Quashmallim or Hedge Ghosts; based on the ephemeral entity rules but also diverging from the core ephemeral rules to fit their respective games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 11-12-2021, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T16:56:36-08:00","id":1467613,"title":"","content":"An interesting note we have two examples of angels knowing embeds as numen<br /> <br /> DtD 366 shatter<br /> DSTG 107, special someone<br /> <br /> But ya, overwhelmingly they do use numen as standard for ephemeral creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T14:48:26-08:00","id":1468428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1467613#post1467613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting note we have two examples of angels knowing embeds as numen<br /> <br /> DtD 366 shatter<br /> DSTG 107, special someone<br /> <br /> But ya, overwhelmingly they do use numen as standard for ephemeral creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that Embeds are more like natural parts of reality to an angel. When they interact with it, the book example is &quot;you know a loose board in a fence provides an opening. A dog, however, goes through it and believes it's always been that way.&quot; Basically as far as angels know, the deep pockets embed isn't them tapping into some reality mainframe, it's that their pockets could always hold that.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting if this sort of thing could play out. A big part of being a spy is checking routines and such. Perhaps it could be a gameplay element to spy on angels and see how their Embeds work out, and then find a way to stop them from accessing them (going back to the example, such as fixing the board so the dog can't get through)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T17:11:33-08:00","id":1468439,"title":"","content":"They are described that way Primial but that's mostly flavour text which does seem to be explored which is sadly a common thing in demon especially when it comes to angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-27T02:52:48-08:00","id":1468964,"title":"","content":"After having read - and started to create Angels for my Campaign - I really feel like some rules of the Ephemereal beings don't really work that well for Angels, limiting what they can and can't do far too much. I think they'd work better if they were more unique, like the Strix are for Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T23:42:26-08:00","id":1474259,"title":"","content":"A few ideas I've had about the next edition.<br /> <br /> 1. Powers of the Occult Matrix- give a little more life to infrastructure. Create mechanics for certain Outputs used by various infrastructures. Give Storytellers a place to start in creating their own. As a bonus, this could double as rules for effects Demons or humans could create if they try to build their own occult matrixes. You could expand the system for glitches to include the nasty side effects a juryrigged matrix crafted by a non-divine intelligence will surely have on reality.<br /> <br /> 2. Mechanists- the God-Machine Chronicles briefly alludes to a group of mortals that steal pieces of the god machine and tinker with them. Expand on this. Maybe certain humans have been hacking the god machine for years, writing elaborate strings of divine source code easily mistaken for magical circles and seals popular in the Renaissance. Use the suggested rules above for making occult matrixes to showcase their abilities. Perhaps some of these hackers have &quot;spells&quot; that can induce a kind of Fall in an Angel but with the baked in component that the resultant demon must obey the mechanist instead- this game's version of a demon summoner. Freeing these captured demons without alerting the god-machine might be an interesting story.<br /> <br /> 3. Inferno- Demon the Descent has been oddly shy about talking about the &quot;other&quot; demons in the chronicles of darkness. I feel like the Inferno from the first edition sourcebook of the same name would make a good added element to the game, a secondary antagonist independent of the god-machine. Perhaps the Inferno is the end result of the Satan Signal that has occasionally been mentioned in the game, a cosmic computer virus that 'infects' reality with a whisper that spreads sin and corruption that slowly grows into an increasingly powerful entity. Perhaps these are the Second Children the Pain Prophet mentions in the original story about the god-machine. Perhaps the &quot;demons&quot; of Inferno are the remnants of human psyches that still linger in the cosmic &quot;recycling bin&quot; of the universe's desktop after the god-machine grinds up their bodies and souls to create essence for itself. I especially like that last one, since it makes a third dangerous elements out of the humans that Demons and the Machine both use and manipulate in their cold war.<br /> <br /> 4. Splintered realities- As a general rule I think the more alternate histories and splintered timelines are used in the game the better.<br /> <br /> 5. The Furies- I really, really want more of the Pain Prophecy to play a role in the overall setting, including more exploration about what the Furies are and how they relate to demons. <br /> <br /> 6. Society- Yeah, the old vampire games left me biased in this regard. I prefer my monstrous entities to have well developed secretive societies surrounding them. The Agendas and Agencies are criminally underdeveloped in the current setting. Angels have been falling since (presumably) the dawn of time. They've had a long time to develop factions, traditions and rivalries. If the Agendas are essentially ideologies in pursuit of Hell then it would make sense that each would have sub-factions pursuing more concrete plans in keeping with that philosophy. In this I'd also like to see the concepts of espionage and...well, being a demon explored in more depth. The first one is straight forward- we are told that espionage culture is a inspiration for the game but aren't given much exploration ABOUT espionage culture or how that is molded into demonic society. How do the Agendas recruit? Who serve as the handlers for a new ring? Who are the leaders? Who are the cutouts? What information is each Agenda looking for, what do they do with it, etc. I'd like to see goals for each Agenda outside of their relationship to the god-machine, for instance. Give us more causes to fight for and plots to foil between the Agendas. Multiply the intrigues. What does a demonic safe house look like? What do you call neutral ground in the world of the Descent? Are Demons who have unlocked their Ciphers given any special treatment in their society? Are there any known demons who have achieved hell? Do they have Demons who are trying to emulate them? Are they a threat? <br /> <br /> 7. Personally, I'd like Demon the Descent to feel more...demonic. A personal opinion, of course, but the setting just never scratched that itch for a creature of sin and malice risen from the depths of hell vibe I was expecting. At least not enough for my taste. I'd like to see hints of the kind of ruthlessness and desperation in the Agendas and Agencies that would have inspired the human understanding of what makes a demon a demon and hell hell, if you follow me. Maybe Saboteurs have secret site devoted to interrogation and torture that inspired the notion that hell is a place of agony and suffering. Maybe mortals tempted into acts of depravity and sin are actually being coaxed away from the plot the god machine has crafted for them. Maybe Aether leaves the stench of brimstone behind when it is used. There are a thousand little ways to explore the idea and a wide range of cultures to draw upon for inspiration. Just...keep descending into that darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T14:30:51-08:00","id":1474439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1474259#post1474259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few ideas I've had about the next edition.<br /> <br /> 1. Powers of the Occult Matrix- give a little more life to infrastructure. Create mechanics for certain Outputs used by various infrastructures. Give Storytellers a place to start in creating their own. As a bonus, this could double as rules for effects Demons or humans could create if they try to build their own occult matrixes. You could expand the system for glitches to include the nasty side effects a juryrigged matrix crafted by a non-divine intelligence will surely have on reality.<br /> <br /> 2. Mechanists- the God-Machine Chronicles briefly alludes to a group of mortals that steal pieces of the god machine and tinker with them. Expand on this. Maybe certain humans have been hacking the god machine for years, writing elaborate strings of divine source code easily mistaken for magical circles and seals popular in the Renaissance. Use the suggested rules above for making occult matrixes to showcase their abilities. Perhaps some of these hackers have &quot;spells&quot; that can induce a kind of Fall in an Angel but with the baked in component that the resultant demon must obey the mechanist instead- this game's version of a demon summoner. Freeing these captured demons without alerting the god-machine might be an interesting story.<br /> <br /> 3. Inferno- Demon the Descent has been oddly shy about talking about the &quot;other&quot; demons in the chronicles of darkness. I feel like the Inferno from the first edition sourcebook of the same name would make a good added element to the game, a secondary antagonist independent of the god-machine. Perhaps the Inferno is the end result of the Satan Signal that has occasionally been mentioned in the game, a cosmic computer virus that 'infects' reality with a whisper that spreads sin and corruption that slowly grows into an increasingly powerful entity. Perhaps these are the Second Children the Pain Prophet mentions in the original story about the god-machine. Perhaps the &quot;demons&quot; of Inferno are the remnants of human psyches that still linger in the cosmic &quot;recycling bin&quot; of the universe's desktop after the god-machine grinds up their bodies and souls to create essence for itself. I especially like that last one, since it makes a third dangerous elements out of the humans that Demons and the Machine both use and manipulate in their cold war.<br /> <br /> 4. Splintered realities- As a general rule I think the more alternate histories and splintered timelines are used in the game the better.<br /> <br /> 5. The Furies- I really, really want more of the Pain Prophecy to play a role in the overall setting, including more exploration about what the Furies are and how they relate to demons. <br /> <br /> 6. Society- Yeah, the old vampire games left me biased in this regard. I prefer my monstrous entities to have well developed secretive societies surrounding them. The Agendas and Agencies are criminally underdeveloped in the current setting. Angels have been falling since (presumably) the dawn of time. They've had a long time to develop factions, traditions and rivalries. If the Agendas are essentially ideologies in pursuit of Hell then it would make sense that each would have sub-factions pursuing more concrete plans in keeping with that philosophy. In this I'd also like to see the concepts of espionage and...well, being a demon explored in more depth. The first one is straight forward- we are told that espionage culture is a inspiration for the game but aren't given much exploration ABOUT espionage culture or how that is molded into demonic society. How do the Agendas recruit? Who serve as the handlers for a new ring? Who are the leaders? Who are the cutouts? What information is each Agenda looking for, what do they do with it, etc. I'd like to see goals for each Agenda outside of their relationship to the god-machine, for instance. Give us more causes to fight for and plots to foil between the Agendas. Multiply the intrigues. What does a demonic safe house look like? What do you call neutral ground in the world of the Descent? Are Demons who have unlocked their Ciphers given any special treatment in their society? Are there any known demons who have achieved hell? Do they have Demons who are trying to emulate them? Are they a threat? <br /> <br /> 7. Personally, I'd like Demon the Descent to feel more...demonic. A personal opinion, of course, but the setting just never scratched that itch for a creature of sin and malice risen from the depths of hell vibe I was expecting. At least not enough for my taste. I'd like to see hints of the kind of ruthlessness and desperation in the Agendas and Agencies that would have inspired the human understanding of what makes a demon a demon and hell hell, if you follow me. Maybe Saboteurs have secret site devoted to interrogation and torture that inspired the notion that hell is a place of agony and suffering. Maybe mortals tempted into acts of depravity and sin are actually being coaxed away from the plot the god machine has crafted for them. Maybe Aether leaves the stench of brimstone behind when it is used. There are a thousand little ways to explore the idea and a wide range of cultures to draw upon for inspiration. Just...keep descending into that darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry if innaporpiate, but I'd like to voice some things I disagree with<br /> <br /> 3. I think the Inferno being expanded through Demon the Descent is a bad idea. It would dilute the focus on what &quot;demons&quot; are for the gameline and possibly bring up and old argument about Descent demons not really being demons despite all the parallels they share. Not only that, but Inferno demons should stay as separate from the machine. The Inferno sourcebook was amazing, and provides a more classical take on demons. To tie them into the God machine or Descent in any way would be a disservice.<br /> <br /> 6. This clashes with the themes of Demon. It's an espionage game filled with backstabbing and liars. And demons aren't the establishment. They are runaways out for their own hides. They don't have any good reason to centralize to such a degree, not to mention it would be a nightmare logistically. The furthest it goes is Agencies (which should be expanded on admittedly), which are ultimately made to benefit individual rings who have SOME trust. in short, having them come together in societies not only makes little sense to lore, but undercuts huge thematics of the game. However, I do agree with some things needing expanding on<br /> <br /> Now the next two I'm iffy about.<br /> <br /> 5. Honestly don't even remember who the Pain Prophet is, but I'm not sure a meta plot is a good thing, though mummy and hunter have a tiny one now, so who knows<br /> <br /> 7. I actually agree with this. While I defend the Descent as most certainly reimagining demons while staying true to them at the same time, I feel the gameline sticks far too much into the spy aspect with it, not only with the terminology but the overall presentation of the game. Granted, I think its a presentation issue more than anything else, but I'm all for it getting more demonic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-11-2022, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T17:55:26-08:00","id":1474460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1474439#post1474439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. I think the Inferno being expanded through Demon the Descent is a bad idea. It would dilute the focus on what &quot;demons&quot; are for the gameline and possibly bring up and old argument about Descent demons not really being demons despite all the parallels they share. Not only that, but Inferno demons should stay as separate from the machine. The Inferno sourcebook was amazing, and provides a more classical take on demons. To tie them into the God machine or Descent in any way would be a disservice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like, there's room to argue that bits of the Machine benefit the Inferno \u2014 it's a diverse being whose medium is Structure Itself invested in maintaining a status quo where the powerful stay powerful and the downtrodden stay downtrodden and abuse and depravity continue behind the scenes, I think we can safely conclude God has uses for Abaddon's oldest crustiest bastards, to say nothing of the possibility of Saboteurs and Tempters taking notes on Slayers and Subversives \u2014 but the safeguards that make Falls the product of individual decisions and the nature of the Machine itself as something to which angels can reasonably point as assured immunity to becoming the basis for Diaboli or Dominions both indicate that marrying the two further is inadvisable.<br /> <br /> Messing about with the splat's blurry take on identity through stuff like Demon House, nonhuman Covers, and several Mundane Embeds contrasted against the increasing individuality of higher Primum, along with perhaps making the stigmata of a given demon's induced stigmatics a little more of a maker's mark, could help get into some of the corruptive angle Inferno and Vampire already offer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6. This clashes with the themes of Demon. It's an espionage game filled with backstabbing and liars. And demons aren't the establishment. They are runaways out for their own hides. They don't have any good reason to centralize to such a degree, not to mention it would be a nightmare logistically. The furthest it goes is Agencies (which should be expanded on admittedly), which are ultimately made to benefit individual rings who have SOME trust. in short, having them come together in societies not only makes little sense to lore, but undercuts huge thematics of the game. However, I do agree with some things needing expanding on </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Vampire gets to have a big developed interconnected society because Institutional Corruption and the All-Night Society basically <i>are</i> the vampiric otherworld, but Demon PCs share a narrative niche with Deviants, and like the Remade, the Unchained don't have the luxury of an assumed semi-open set of connections to pull on, because their primary opposition has a stronger grasp on those things by virtue of not being what the PCs are.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the default answer to &quot;What is the Satan Signal?&quot; is &quot;side-effect of a fucked-up cryptid that gets a lot of places it shouldn't be&quot; rather than &quot;a Big Demon out there in the world has made it a point to Free Demonkind&quot; \u2014 like Mage, Demon's view of the Chronicles is not only a Gnostic perspective, but a perspective in which enlightenment/freedom from the world is a strictly personal achievement (and therefore &quot;fuck you, got mine&quot; is in full effect for many characters in pursuit of it, since you can't share it and trying might actually cause you to lose it).<br /> <br /> Setting aside Agencies for the moment,* it'd be good to get a little more detail on squads and associations, since it builds out some of the usual channels of communication between the Unchained and &quot;cross-ring group of demons with a shared Agenda&quot; has the same kind of potential for fun clashing-loyalties/distrustful heist-crew issues as lodges provide for packs in Werewolf 2e.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Provided examples make it pretty clear they run the gamut in roles from Consilium-analogues to freehold-analogues to Ordo Dracul chapterhouse analogues to small-scale Hunter compact analogues, all of which boils down to &quot;a group of demons larger than a single ring have pooled their skills and/or resources in some way toward a particular end,&quot; which isn't a description that strictly requires there to be demons and in fact can totally have no actual demons at all, courtesy of the Machine's observed capacity to use angels and exiles as snare-traps and infiltrators.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7. I actually agree with this. While I defend the Descent as most certainly reimagining demons while staying true to them at the same time, I feel the gameline sticks far too much into the soy aspect with it, not only with the terminology but the overall presentation of the game. Granted, I think its a presentation issue more than anything else, but I'm all for it getting more demonic </div> </div> </div>I think Mortal Remains and the Contagion material has made a decent case for how Descent can present the Unchained without losing the more Gnostic take on angels and demons.<br /> <br /> Putting more attention on psyops would go a long way, I imagine, not least because it brings added prominence to trying to engineer Falls, trying to steer people into being amenable to pacts, and trying to turn people against the Machine's projects.<br /> <br /> In general, I've said it elsewhere and it merits repeating: demons don't go in for mythologizing so much, but their interface with humanity sure does and it helps to have examples of that when the truth is so ruinous to the Unchained constitution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T20:01:35-08:00","id":1474473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1474460#post1474460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, there's room to argue that bits of the Machine benefit the Inferno \u2014 it's a diverse being whose medium is Structure Itself invested in maintaining a status quo where the powerful stay powerful and the downtrodden stay downtrodden and abuse and depravity continue behind the scenes, I think we can safely conclude God has uses for Abaddon's oldest crustiest bastards, to say nothing of the possibility of Saboteurs and Tempters taking notes on Slayers and Subversives \u2014 but the safeguards that make Falls the product of individual decisions and the nature of the Machine itself as something to which angels can reasonably point as assured immunity to becoming the basis for Diaboli or Dominions both indicate that marrying the two further is inadvisable.<br /> <br /> Messing about with the splat's blurry take on identity through stuff like Demon House, nonhuman Covers, and several Mundane Embeds contrasted against the increasing individuality of higher Primum, along with perhaps making the stigmata of a given demon's induced stigmatics a little more of a maker's mark, could help get into some of the corruptive angle Inferno and Vampire already offer.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Vampire gets to have a big developed interconnected society because Institutional Corruption and the All-Night Society basically <i>are</i> the vampiric otherworld, but Demon PCs share a narrative niche with Deviants, and like the Remade, the Unchained don't have the luxury of an assumed semi-open set of connections to pull on, because their primary opposition has a stronger grasp on those things by virtue of not being what the PCs are.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the default answer to &amp;quot;What is the Satan Signal?&amp;quot; is &amp;quot;side-effect of a fucked-up cryptid that gets a lot of places it shouldn't be&amp;quot; rather than &amp;quot;a Big Demon out there in the world has made it a point to Free Demonkind&amp;quot; \u2014 like Mage, Demon's view of the Chronicles is not only a Gnostic perspective, but a perspective in which enlightenment/freedom from the world is a strictly personal achievement (and therefore &amp;quot;fuck you, got mine&amp;quot; is in full effect for many characters in pursuit of it, since you can't share it and trying might actually cause you to lose it).<br /> <br /> Setting aside Agencies for the moment,* it'd be good to get a little more detail on squads and associations, since it builds out some of the usual channels of communication between the Unchained and &amp;quot;cross-ring group of demons with a shared Agenda&amp;quot; has the same kind of potential for fun clashing-loyalties/distrustful heist-crew issues as lodges provide for packs in Werewolf 2e.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*Provided examples make it pretty clear they run the gamut in roles from Consilium-analogues to freehold-analogues to Ordo Dracul chapterhouse analogues to small-scale Hunter compact analogues, all of which boils down to &amp;quot;a group of demons larger than a single ring have pooled their skills and/or resources in some way toward a particular end,&amp;quot; which isn't a description that strictly requires there to be demons and in fact can totally have no actual demons at all, courtesy of the Machine's observed capacity to use angels and exiles as snare-traps and infiltrators.</span><br /> <br /> I think Mortal Remains and the Contagion material has made a decent case for how Descent can present the Unchained without losing the more Gnostic take on angels and demons.<br /> <br /> Putting more attention on psyops would go a long way, I imagine, not least because it brings added prominence to trying to engineer Falls, trying to steer people into being amenable to pacts, and trying to turn people against the Machine's projects.<br /> <br /> In general, I've said it elsewhere and it merits repeating: demons don't go in for mythologizing so much, but their interface with humanity sure does and it helps to have examples of that when the truth is so ruinous to the Unchained constitution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I have no issue with the Inferno being a potential plot element. I just don't think it's a good idea to make it a by product or the God machine. I think it is to its detriment to do such a thing<br /> <br /> As for everything else, I agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T21:30:21-08:00","id":1474888,"title":"","content":"\u201c3. I think the Inferno being expanded through Demon the Descent is a bad idea. It would dilute the focus on what &quot;demons&quot; are for the gameline and possibly bring up and old argument about Descent demons not really being demons despite all the parallels they share. Not only that, but Inferno demons should stay as separate from the machine. The Inferno sourcebook was amazing, and provides a more classical take on demons. To tie them into the God machine or Descent in any way would be a disservice.\u201d<br /> Shrug. I suppose there is that danger of \u201cdilution\u201d, a problem that is risked when trying to incorporate any established concept into another established one. But I think there are ways to avoid that problem in the hands of a skilled writer. I\u2019ll cite the incorporation of Immortals into Mummy the Curse, first in dark eras and later into the proper release of Mummy\u2019s second edition. One way that I suggested earlier is to let Demon: The Descent be the \u2018fallen angels\u2019 of demonic lore and emphasize Inferno demons as \u2018damned mortal souls\u2019, focusing primarily on whispers, possessed, and Inferno corrupted spirits and ghosts (familiar but twisted concepts established already in the Chronicles and Descent alike) and leave the more powerful entities discussed in Inferno as shadowed rumors (which, to be fair, is not far off from how they are treated in the Inferno book in the first place). Shrug. First edition has largely treated Inferno like the elephant in the room, going to (in my opinion, of course) absurd lengths in the Storyteller\u2019s Guide to even mention groups like Belial\u2019s Brood, Mastigos, the Lucifuge, etc. I don\u2019t feel like mentioning the Qashmallim in the Core book \u2018diluted\u2019 the concept of God-Machine controlled angels, and I don\u2019t think talking about Inferno would do that here.<br /> <br /> \u201c6. This clashes with the themes of Demon.\u201d<br /> I could not disagree with this statement more vehemently.<br /> \u201cIt's an espionage game filled with backstabbing and liars.\u201d<br /> Yes, it is. And I do not believe this fact in any way makes a more well developed demonic society an impossibility. In fact, I\u2019d argue the opposite. More on that in a moment.<br /> \u201cAnd demons aren't the establishment. They are runaways out for their own hides. They don't have any good reason to centralize to such a degree, not to mention it would be a nightmare logistically.\u201d<br /> You don\u2019t need to be the \u2018establishment\u2019 to have organization, traditions, or a society. Some of the most tightly knit communities on Earth come from immigrants and refuges that found themselves in a strange land and had no one but one another to rely upon. And no matter how cautious or paranoid a single person might be, sooner or later somebody is gonna do the math and realize that you will have more success working with people and watching each other\u2019s backs than you will have going it alone when you are being hunted or working clandestinely. The best spy organizations on Earth by necessity have well developed hierarchies, well established protocols for engagement and conducting missions, carefully maintained channels for information and resources, and so on. I would strongly argue that organization is an absolute necessity for long term survival against something like the god machine. Also, I\u2019d like to think that hyper advanced robotic ultra dimensional computer programs, cut off from the main network or not, can handle a higher degree of logistics than us poor dumb humans.<br /> \u201cThe furthest it goes is Agencies (which should be expanded on admittedly), which are ultimately made to benefit individual rings who have SOME trust.\u201d<br /> I don\u2019t even think that statement is true per what we see in first edition. Agencies, from my reading, are left frustratingly ambiguous in size and scope, but at bare minimum most certainly are providing services to and making use of more than a single Ring.<br /> \u201cin short, having them come together in societies not only makes little sense to lore, but undercuts huge thematics of the game.\u201d<br /> And I once again think the exact opposite. A game dealing with espionage and spy culture is, to me, inherently implying a carefully maintained web of secret organizations, working together or competing with each other. We don\u2019t need an elaborate feudal system like Vampire, or the pomp and circumstance of a Changeling Freehold, mind you. I\u2019d imagine Demons are even more focused on layers within layers of secrecy than your average vampire, in fact. I\u2019d propose taking the basic structure of a spy network and reimagining in it in more supernatural terms. A Ring of Demons implies having a handler that feeds them information, resources, and safety in exchange for going on missions. A handler implies a network that demon reports to, which implies a hierarchy with some unknown(s) at the top organizing the overall goals of the Agenda or Agency- a spy master or director. A society composed of face dancer technomonsters implies a need for code words, secret handshakes, and other elaborate systems of identification so that they know you are you no matter who you seem to be on any given day. I see a lot of potential in that alone and I\u2019m surprised it wasn\u2019t explored in more detail in first edition.<br /> \u201c5. Honestly don't even remember who the Pain Prophet is, but I'm not sure a meta plot is a good thing, though mummy and hunter have a tiny one now, so who knows\u201d<br /> Well, bad news, you\u2019ve already got one. The Pain Prophet was the one who wrote the first story about the God-Machine, all the way back in the original rulebook when Chronicles was still called the new world of darkness. He described a floating city controlled by angels that humanity caused to crash into the sea, but 8 surviving angels became the Furies and spoke a series of curses upon mankind similar to the trumpets being sounded during the biblical apocalypse. One of these Furies was death and hid on the far side of the moon. The God-Machine Chronicles and Demon both establish that the body of this Fury or angel or whatever was recovered during the moon landing and is now housed by Deva Corporation. Since we\u2019ve already gone that deep into the meta plot we might as well go all in and explore what these Furies really are within the current framework of Descent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T22:54:39-08:00","id":1474889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1474888#post1474888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Ring of Demons implies having a handler that feeds them information, resources, and safety in exchange for going on missions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've tripped at step one, because this is not what a ring is. A ring is just a small group of demons banding together for mutual protection. That doesn't imply a handler, because individual demons' goals are personal and potentially incompatible and may require no further engagement with the God-Machine's workings than staying out of its way, never mind going on missions as a regular assumed purpose of the group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see a lot of potential in that alone and I\u2019m surprised it wasn\u2019t explored in more detail in first edition. </div> </div> </div>In the corebook alone, there's the entire Organization section of the Tempter writeup, as well as the four pages of sample Agencies and discussion of the four different types of Agency.<br /> <br /> There is an entire section on building Agencies in the Player's Guide, including discussions of different scopes of the three types of non-Compromised Agency and the practices of recruitment and expansion; the PG's section for discussing Tempters in detail also talks about their role in a ring, as well as their networking practices and the way their cults and associations operate, while the section on the Agendas and Incarnations within a ring also establishes in more detail how a squad works and why there isn't much detail given to them as groups.<br /> <br /> The Storyteller's Guide's section on tilting the game toward a particular quadrant of espionage fiction, and the whole Smooth half of that graph has suggestions for playing characters assumed to be part of an Agency.<br /> <br /> It's plenty of detail for a gameline that got all of its books out before the organization rules were put together. As with many other things about a hypothetical new edition, being able to use those rules from the jump would help with mechanically structuring Agencies, but the line's said about as much as need be said as far as establishing the general qualities of a widely variable sort of group that many demons view as risky to form, join, or interact with for the perfectly rational reasons of their old boss being in the world looking for them and being partially built out of <i>the concepts of hierarchy, organization, and routine</i>. Aside from not having the mechanics to model them in significant detail, the main other thing missing from Agencies in 1e was the wordcount-bomb that is More Examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 02-18-2022, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T06:25:09-07:00","id":1521378,"title":"","content":"Reviving it a little bit because I've now 28 sessions as a GM for Demon and there is two glaring things I'd like to see changed someday (hopefully, but I won't hold my breath).<br /> <br /> 1. Integrators. I love them in concept, but they seem to be a very hard sell for most players I've talked about, because they are &quot;sellout&quot; or &quot;dangerous&quot; for them because they fear they'd throw them to the Angels, so to speak. I find it a little sad because that's basically one fourth of the basic potential for the players that's closed off (at least in my group and the very limited pool of D:tD players around them). I think a simple tweak like &quot;they want to change the God-Machine&quot; instead of &quot;they want to become Angels with personnalities and hope it'll change the Machine&quot;. Which frankly would be more a change of perspective rather than a tweak because I feel that's already a necessity of their Agenda.<br /> <br /> 2. Cypher and Pacts need a simplification, because I still haven't finished designing the Interlocks for any players and Pacts are a pain in the bip to play with. Incidentely, I also feels that the interaction between Pacts and Covers should be made a little simpler/smoother, but that may just be because my players are just starting to dabble in all of it so we're rought around the edges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T16:47:26-07:00","id":1522367,"title":"","content":"Well, Ur-Than, I agree with both your points and I hope they get addressed in the next edition. I sincerely wish you luck in getting some good discussion going on those topics. I got driven off a year and a half ago from the combination of condescension and the propensity of people to lecture me about how my ideas for a second edition are &quot;wrong actually&quot; over and over rather than people offering ideas of their own which was my main interest in the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-17T08:19:50-07:00","id":1522706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ur-Than</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1466815-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-2ed-of-the-descent?p=1521378#post1521378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a simple tweak like &quot;they want to change the God-Machine&quot; instead of &quot;they want to become Angels with personnalities and hope it'll change the Machine&quot;. Which frankly would be more a change of perspective rather than a tweak because I feel that's already a necessity of their Agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>The corebook writeup describes the Agenda as splitting into roughly three factions based on its differences in opinion on what the final goal of being an Integrator is. The largest faction wants to reprogram the Machine or rejoin the system with their newfound humanity intact \u2014 the latter method is not &quot;hoping it'll change the Machine&quot; as &quot;aiming to become an internal reformist,&quot; while the former allows for changing the Machine before they rejoin it as an angel. The other two factions are aiming to either get the best of both worlds re: loyalism and the Fall or complete whatever undercover mission they believe they were sent into deep-deep cover for.<br /> <br /> The unifying feature of the Agenda is that Integrators all want to integrate themselves back into the Machine (and thus pick up the skills and development priorities of the Agenda Condition). That's not significantly more dangerous than Saboteurs drawing attention by messing with Infrastructure that can spark disasters or Tempters putting their Agency's lower rungs in harm's way for a goal they don't entirely believe is possible. The Idealists are arguably the second most organized Agenda of the main four, and the highlighted need for most of them to do something more involved than turning themselves in to the nearest recycling station serves the same general function as Inquisitors' recognition that they can't work alone precisely <i>because</i> anything could be a trap \u2014 Angel Empathy's Beat Condition may not be a diegetic phenomenon, but the fact remains that Integrators grow faster when they put their fellows at risk and make themselves suspect and specifically in ways that give them opportunities to advance their Cipher.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Cypher and Pacts need a simplification, because I still haven't finished designing the Interlocks for any players and Pacts are a pain in the bip to play with. Incidentely, I also feels that the interaction between Pacts and Covers should be made a little simpler/smoother, but that may just be because my players are just starting to dabble in all of it so we're rought around the edges. </div> </div> </div>On the one hand, I can definitely agree with this, but on the other hand I feel that Changeling 2e's more freeform system for pledgecraft is not substantially preferable to 1e's extensive balancing act; the former is definitely simpler, but it does not make arbitration easier.<br /> <br /> The bigger problem currently facing demonic pactwork is that the full spread of systems are currently spread across about half a dozen books (including multiple Dark Eras) and also plug into the systems for gadgets (and the gadget mechanics are an iffy mix of well-defined and fiat-based), which itself runs into the problem of pacts currently being notionally a mysterious ability separate from the God-Machine's installed shortcuts and systems, and being the first Revised Storytelling System game out the door is all I can readily attribute several early Embeds and Exploits' comparative lack of specific mechanical effects to.<br /> <br /> Obviously something like Promethean 2e's Pilgrimage charting doesn't work for Demon without changing one of the assumptions of the game, because not every demon pursues the Cipher specifically because it's a loose thread to chase rather than a deliberately constructed goal for themselves, but like &quot;demons and angels use mostly the same rules instead of the latter being mechanically Ephemeral Beings But Not Really,&quot; an overhaul of the splat's mechanical interface to better mess with &quot;things the God-Machine has made true about the world, and their unintended uses&quot; would go a long way.<br /> <br /> The game already incentivizes demons whose main goal is more involved than staying in Cover to pick up a bunch of Embeds both as potential Keys and as routes to developing Exploits, and the sheer breadth of things Exploits can do (including several things that would be equivalent to template features on other splats) makes me inclined to want the Cipher to be part of something stylistically similar to the Sphere Grid from Final Fantasy X or a simplified version of Deviant's conspiracy/Web of Pain mechanics; you can study and/or subvert pieces of Infrastructure to gain knowledge of new tricks that can then serve as the basis for new gadgets or abilities, which in turn can make certain pact benefits less troublesome to provide, which can then make it easier to avoid or mitigate damage to your Cover.<br /> <br /> Given that Deviants run on a somewhat reduced baseline template to account for the granularity of Variation and Scar Magnitude and the inclusion of the conspiracy mechanics, it's possible this might necessitate Cover change to work more like the Resilient Cover hack from the Storyteller's Guide, if not outright replace what the splat's Integrity analogue is like Promethean did, but the core of what I'm saying here, I guess, is that a Demon 2e would benefit greatly from a full ludo-structural overhaul of its powerset to make Demon Powers, including pacts and the Cipher, run in a more unified framework.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-19T00:41:29-07:00","id":1522779,"title":"","content":"This likely has been said before, and is probably quite rambling (I am writing this just before midnight) but for what I'd want as a 2e for Demon;<ul><li>Make Embeds/Exploits both less reliant on die rolls, and also not have such terrible consequences for dramatic failures.</li> </ul>The fact that any Embed roll can fail is one thing, as you're going to be making an attempt to basically use a jury rigged access to the God-Machine's little tricks. However, <i>Exploits</i> failing means you're burning up aether for an attempt (which among the supernatural fuels is one of the hardest to get conveniently, as far as I can tell) and potentially risking Compromise, or burning up aether <i>and</i> wasting a point willpower, which can arguably be harder to get back depending on the circumstances. On top of that, the consequences for getting a dramatic failure on either sets of abilities is often far in excess of the benefits of a single beat - some of them can be funny to run through, but things like all the items in your pocket vanishing forever or becoming automatically on the God-Machine's radar and needing to do <i>drastic action <b><u>now</u></b></i> (In My Pocket and Interference, both Embeds) are just a pain nine times out of ten. (and that's presuming you willingly get a dramatic failure, and weren't forced into it by an outside power)<br /> <br /> I think borrowing from Changeling's book and making certain Embeds/Exploits outright just work when activated would resolve at least some of this issue, especially with the addition of an &quot;activate safely to get a minor benefit, roll to get a bigger one but have the risk of it failing and thus bad things happening&quot; mechanic. Which leads into my next desire for Demon;<ul><li>More consolidation on Embeds, and expansion of their die pools.</li> </ul>The list of Embeds is staggeringly broad, even if they're mostly set in just two books, and most of them have a unique effect with <i>some</i> overlap between them (powers that affect die rolls, powers that force a success with a complication for it, etc). However, most of these effects are very niche with some being overtly useful (it's rare that Alibi and Interference won't get taken, Download Knowledge and Fungible Knowledge are good even if you roll poorly for them, and In My Pocket is the only reason I got through one particular campaign). Even with how cheap getting Embeds are compared to most supernaturals (and even most merits, in terms of versatility) it feels odd to have so many powers that are so disparate in their utility, especially since all the ones that are practically &quot;essential&quot; to have are ones that have particular die pools that won't work across every character. This results in a complicated issue (combined with the issue noted below), in that you can have a bunch of powers yo want but they simply don't work with your character because you need to roll to activate near anything that isn't a form power.<br /> <br /> Further, there are a lot of different Skills that don't get utilized much for Embeds. Computers, Occult, Drive, Academics, Animal Ken, Expression, even Medicine from my memory don't get much utility in a list of over a hundred. It feels very... unbalanced is all. Which leads into;<ul><li>Wits should not be the most important attribute you could ever have.</li> </ul>No doubts about it, if there's one attribute you do not want to go small on, it's Wits. You need it for Cipher checks, Compromise rolls, Aetheric Resonance's merits are related to having at least a higher than the human average in, and over half the embeds in the listing use it, and that's before the normal benefits for having a good Wits attribute come in that literally anyone else benefits from. To a lesser extent Manipulation is likewise an important trait to have, given it's also in Cipher checks and a healthy amount of Embed attribute rolls... but Wits is disproportionately high. On the one hand, yes, this is a spy game so a character having a good Wits is good. On the other hand, it means that any character who is physically focused is going to be a <i>far</i> worse off Demon than one that focuses on Wits simply because they're going to average far worse on Demon specific survival things. Even one of the best ranged form powers to have, Rivet Arm (very long range, high damage, crafting utility on top of firepower), is Wits based and not Dexterity.<br /> <br /> This ties into the above issue with Embeds in that there is a very real issue of there being a wrong way to make a Demon character mechanically before you even get into choosing Embeds and Exploits, which feels... wrong for a Chronicles of Darkness game. Sure, there are sensible ways to make characters, but needing to orient yourself based on particular attributes like you're making a D&amp;D character really hurts character diversity if you're actually going to be getting into the thick of Infrastructure and Angels. I would decouple things like Compromise and Interlock discoveries from Wits, or at least make it the higher of a few options so players have options when rolling. If nothing else it'd help me make up characters that are people and not just high Wits takers.<ul><li>Incarnations are pointless barring Analysts.</li> </ul>This one is unrelated to the above, but unless you take an Analyst there is nothing stopping you from building a Demon the exact same way as a Destroyer, a Guardian, a Messenger or a Psychopomp, and playing them the same way. All the prerequisites you have for playing any of them are just to take an Embed from their particular school of Embed... and that's it. There are no benefits or drawbacks for taking a particular Incarnation beyond Going Loud (where you get all Embeds from a particular school) and the Monkey Wrencher merit - while both of these are useful in their own ways, if you're Going Loud things have definitely gone wrong in a real way and Monkey Wrencher needs you to actively buy it in order to use it. It doesn't feel like Incarnation has a point if the only impact it's going to have is either roleplay related or something that needs an active investment to get any benefit from, and they all do pretty much the exact same thing but with a slightly different flavour (and no assurance any of those powers will help, since almost every Embed doesn't even refer to Primum).<br /> <br /> Analyst, on the other hand, changes things; you get to choose an Exploit from the list without any prerequisites needing to be met, and when you Go Loud you have a superpower that lets you play around and do some really crazy stuff (if with some setup). My last Demon game had three players choosing to play an Analyst simply because they stuck out and had an active benefit compared to any of the other Incarnations, which is ironic since Analysts are supposed to be relatively rare (or at least self aware ones are). Giving some exclusive ability to any of the main Incarnations would help them stand out, even if it's to make them have a discount to purchasing their own specialty of Embeds (though preferably more than that).<br /> <br /> <br /> That's all I can think on at the moment, and I hope this was... at least somewhat conductive to the overall discussion. Again, sorry if this is all stuff that has been touched on before with more eloquence. Just late tonight and these issues have bugged me for a good while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}